"0ce73380-2abe-591b-a501-2fffb25e9869" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284895} {:answer/id #uuid "1b175e13-968e-5ec8-9d17-0a77d893b075" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285027} {:answer/id #uuid "2e9105f8-f2d6-5c3f-9c60-b593e96c51d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285206} {:answer/id #uuid "ab82b635-2160-5ed5-a7f7-47c54a617da1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286354} {:answer/id #uuid "ace7fdea-5fb7-5fd8-aa32-30d01d52a4f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ace7fdea-5fb7-5fd8-aa32-30d01d52a4f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286368} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1b35598-0d81-58f5-9d4e-8b067b0830b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287516}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9a99808d-9449-580d-ae70-e6aff48c1ff9" :question/math-academy-id "q-20004" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $h=⟨2,0,3⟩$ and $l=⟨4,1,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h\\times l & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 3)i-(2\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 3)j+(2\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-3i+6j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-3,6,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,h\\times l\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292813 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ba6a314-9690-51f8-ac65-d87aa7adaabd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291309}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ba6a314-9690-51f8-ac65-d87aa7adaabd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291309} :answer-field/id #uuid "de32afac-e614-53fa-b799-24f12769f89d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292428}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc161987-10e4-5ee6-a6c6-ed110201a1f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-275220" :question/problem "Calculate the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $a=⟨-4,-2,1⟩$ and $b=⟨0,-2,-1⟩.$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 1)i-((-4)\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 1)j+((-4)\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =4i-4j+8k \\\\  & =⟨4,-4,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292814 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff2a44dc-fdc6-559d-9985-a9e6ce7b18ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291722}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff2a44dc-fdc6-559d-9985-a9e6ce7b18ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291722} :answer-field/id #uuid "60989695-b200-54ed-9968-72677234d5ec" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292028}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c7348e7-1921-5e09-8018-775e68160619" :question/math-academy-id "q-275222" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the triangle spanned by $a=⟨-2,-1,0⟩$ and $b=⟨-4,2,-2⟩.$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 0)i-((-2)\\cdot (-2)-(-4)\\cdot 0)j+((-2)\\cdot 2-(-4)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =2i-4j-8k \\\\  & =⟨2,-4,-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{2}=\\sqrt{21}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297464 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e27d4c6-c946-503d-ac45-3010dc21b71f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e27d4c6-c946-503d-ac45-3010dc21b71f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296023} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c1cb17d-1226-50b5-8a55-fa9762362774" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296861}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e9963779-43cf-5b65-8821-6ff0b678d8cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-316345" :question/problem "Calculate the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $a=⟨-3,5,0⟩$ and $b=⟨4,-1,2⟩.$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-1))i-((-3)\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 4)j+((-3)\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =10i+6j-17k \\\\  & =⟨10,6,-17⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-17)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+36+289} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{425} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297465 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ed164a80-8e70-5398-881b-db2dc37213b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ed164a80-8e70-5398-881b-db2dc37213b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296523} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa7793f2-af09-5083-a758-5dedb4543d5e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297147}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b9773af-f53a-5ffd-bd89-0fdc3a8398e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-316350" :question/problem "Calculate the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $a=⟨1,0,0⟩$ and $b=⟨0,3,4⟩.$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 3)i-(1\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 0)j+(1\\cdot 3-0\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =0i-4j+3k \\\\  & =⟨0,-4,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297466 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62f41066-5228-5f44-a4bc-f9a7a9de4308" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295832}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62f41066-5228-5f44-a4bc-f9a7a9de4308" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295832} :answer-field/id #uuid "809afc0c-e441-5baf-a7b0-01f0a22f4f33" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296898}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ed3e1530-1ab9-5085-9128-11a28820fcba" :question/math-academy-id "q-316355" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the triangle spanned by $p=⟨0,5,-1⟩$ and $q=⟨6,0,1⟩.$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\times q & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)i-(0\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 6)j+(0\\cdot 0-5\\cdot 6)k \\\\  & =5i-6j-30k \\\\  & =⟨5,-6,-30⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,p\\times q\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-30)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+36+900} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{961} \\\\  & =31.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{31}{2}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Triangle Spanned by Two Vectors"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105733 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105591 :question/id #uuid "e354c43b-837f-5447-9759-6aeb3952cd57" :question/math-academy-id "e-4345" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC,$ if $A(1,0,-2),$ $B(-2,0,1),$ $C(1,1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2i+k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i+j-k)-(i-2k) \\\\  & =j+k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 1)i-(-3\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 0)j+(-3\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-3i+3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106122 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85a14407-0a6c-560b-8095-289da4451e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102609} {:answer/id #uuid "b2030633-b210-501b-9cf0-3ba099309103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102610} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b9134c-bdf1-524b-a131-a0f0eeff5541" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102611} {:answer/id #uuid "0905aefd-9fae-531d-b65e-a331cd656d3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102612} {:answer/id #uuid "4a088302-e129-5ad6-bedd-5373b57c8359" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102613}] :answer-field/id #uuid "74b45571-7029-59a9-a139-4dde30284cc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102608}] :question/id #uuid "b7fa7f1d-963f-5878-b4cb-ed2a7ee6c561" :question/math-academy-id "q-20016" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△ABC$, if $A(1, 1, 0)$, $B(3, 2, 2)$, $C(1, 2, 1)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106123 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e79b7a5-a889-5636-81a6-5c628d9606ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284912} {:answer/id #uuid "78d9ff09-0da1-5a53-8355-bac5cd8c3dc2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285912} {:answer/id #uuid "a718ab84-4198-545d-bdfa-d0f5048065c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286310} {:answer/id #uuid "b63ac272-c912-57b7-9e69-82262d25e7e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286451} {:answer/id #uuid "e47df95b-3077-5100-92fa-f72c23d2e1f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286879}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e79b7a5-a889-5636-81a6-5c628d9606ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284912} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b4dc220-3cdd-52b1-9314-1cc837d05799" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287270}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7799a52e-21d3-584f-93c3-f00bb69321c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-20026" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,PQR$, if $P(4,7,3)$, $Q(5,6,2)$, $R(3,8,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(5i+6j+2k)-(4i+7j+3k) \\\\  & =i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(3i+8j+3k)-(4i+7j+3k) \\\\  & =-i+j \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1))i-(1\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-1))j+(1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =i+j \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "180fef8e-8ea9-590e-9071-b52b4ff39f1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{62}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260084} {:answer/id #uuid "26d80b3f-6ec0-5698-94d6-f4acd16ceac0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{31}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260215} {:answer/id #uuid "86077a7b-20d4-5ba1-ac9f-2d5a7c49bd94" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261039} {:answer/id #uuid "8d5c1838-c93e-5dfd-a8b4-ee4f539e435b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{31}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261110} {:answer/id #uuid "c792e5c1-7724-54f5-bafa-ba70e9aeab23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c792e5c1-7724-54f5-bafa-ba70e9aeab23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261641} :answer-field/id #uuid "6dd7393b-e016-5b2f-a010-b9d7e2bb709b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262303}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6f81e690-5559-586b-a65b-10e4fedf8848" :question/math-academy-id "q-127866" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,ABC,$ if $A(5,0,5),$ $B(6,-1,4),$ $C(9,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(6i-j+4k)-(5i+5k) \\\\  & =i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(9i+j)-(5i+5k) \\\\  & =4i+j-5k \\\\  & =⟨4,1,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot (-1))i-(1\\cdot (-5)-4\\cdot (-1))j+(1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =6i+j+5k \\\\  & =⟨6,1,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{5}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{62}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e7e2ae-f229-5350-bfe1-691c383da5a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259879} {:answer/id #uuid "4884595d-d50d-5093-a9bb-f114519d1405" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{17}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260502} {:answer/id #uuid "93fa82e9-537b-5d8c-9b2e-dd7bafe5cff8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261162} {:answer/id #uuid "c4a6eb21-de86-596c-8e62-5108683c8e7b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261611} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6f234a-fdc5-5088-b8f4-93467b60aada" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93fa82e9-537b-5d8c-9b2e-dd7bafe5cff8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261162} :answer-field/id #uuid "38599921-2cac-5ba2-a213-10d43c1e348b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262224}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e1c91586-572d-5c90-b62f-69027efa2214" :question/math-academy-id "q-127908" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,PQR,$ if $P(2,6,6),$ $Q(4,8,2),$ $R(0,5,6).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(4i+8j+2k)-(2i+6j+6k) \\\\  & =2i+2j-4k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,-4⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(5j+6k)-(2i+6j+6k) \\\\  & =-2i-j \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-4))i-(2\\cdot 0-(-2)\\cdot (-4))j+(2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-4i+8j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-4,8,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{8}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{84} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{2}=\\sqrt{21}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262848 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "622785b6-0e5a-504c-8ba7-61c896b4597d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260722} {:answer/id #uuid "679872d9-fa42-5cab-a5a3-e29f317c39aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{21\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260780} {:answer/id #uuid "8c028d49-b914-543f-9314-9b33da7f6f9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{86}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261098} {:answer/id #uuid "c1ddb50b-ce6a-5a57-9ddd-5fad6c4d0a87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{13}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261586} {:answer/id #uuid "cd0039be-579d-518d-a9d0-03877c66d22e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{43}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c028d49-b914-543f-9314-9b33da7f6f9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{86}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261098} :answer-field/id #uuid "8005319e-8e8b-5ab9-a565-7a8f41f83817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262339}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ef5f09ae-6eb9-5c04-9bb6-e694acc7855a" :question/math-academy-id "q-127913" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,PQR,$ if $P(6,1,5),$ $Q(5,1,7),$ $R(4,2,0).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(5i+j+7k)-(6i+j+5k) \\\\  & =-i+2k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(4i+2j)-(6i+j+5k) \\\\  & =-2i+j-5k \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,-5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot (-5)-1\\cdot 2)i-((-1)\\cdot (-5)-(-2)\\cdot 2)j+((-1)\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-2i-9j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-9,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-9)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{86}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{86}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262849 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "391e4ba1-cf5b-5a61-85aa-0b17144eae39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260382} {:answer/id #uuid "668cda2c-92ee-5199-b862-983b8a4c4afb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260768} {:answer/id #uuid "6c2dfdd4-a52e-57e2-9f5e-3ab0a20c414b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260822} {:answer/id #uuid "6cb8fe9f-e32c-520a-816f-56dd8fde1270" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260832} {:answer/id #uuid "8671701c-63a1-5620-a70a-e58d9e0297c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261044}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "668cda2c-92ee-5199-b862-983b8a4c4afb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260768} :answer-field/id #uuid "8368d079-5a01-5ee1-9848-effbe38c3053" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262345}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1ecbe45d-cebe-5d0b-b79b-4337a04e8ef8" :question/math-academy-id "q-127915" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,WXY,$ if $W(3,9,4),$ $X(1,7,3),$ $Y(6,12,8).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX} & =x-w \\\\  & =(i+7j+3k)-(3i+9j+4k) \\\\  & =-2i-2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =y-w \\\\  & =(6i+12j+8k)-(3i+9j+4k) \\\\  & =3i+3j+4k \\\\  & =⟨3,3,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-1))i-((-2)\\cdot 4-3\\cdot (-1))j+((-2)\\cdot 3-3\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-5i+5j \\\\  & =⟨-5,5,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+{5}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,WXY$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{5\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1920d715-e444-516d-8fac-793798266f68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285011} {:answer/id #uuid "29e1177a-6728-5e48-bee7-8dc0e9fdc691" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285154} {:answer/id #uuid "a7af1a98-7783-53e1-8fd7-c75ee0dc0fa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286317} {:answer/id #uuid "af7def2a-51b9-5a38-89f0-dcfcbe125b08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286387} {:answer/id #uuid "f54aae70-dfb4-5043-9686-2b5185587d3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f54aae70-dfb4-5043-9686-2b5185587d3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287034} :answer-field/id #uuid "da1704eb-bbb3-5f38-b0f6-6aae59a45a8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287592}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "20a90ebb-b81e-5c2a-8135-e658aa05c005" :question/math-academy-id "q-18581" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,LMN$, if $L(0,0,1)$, $M(2,1,1)$, $N(3,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-k \\\\  & =2i+j \\\\  & =⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(3i+j+k)-k \\\\  & =3i+j \\\\  & =⟨3,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 1)i-(2\\cdot 0-0\\cdot 3)j+(2\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =-k \\\\  & =⟨0,0,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03d78b70-cb8f-5e6f-99ce-03eb325a6129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284818} {:answer/id #uuid "0586a3e6-6eb5-5101-969f-81fc47045d2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284833} {:answer/id #uuid "57c889db-8102-5c28-aa33-9a91e2b2a89f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285591} {:answer/id #uuid "bcba07e4-2097-5048-b82d-fcda445cced9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286508} {:answer/id #uuid "c3c8ab1c-911c-552c-9f08-414eae7622f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286582}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03d78b70-cb8f-5e6f-99ce-03eb325a6129" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284818} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c509f79-9189-5afb-8b33-24e72c7a6b3a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287374}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cee105b4-e3ae-5a95-a3ab-a9f9dc2703a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-20017" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,RST$, if $R(3,-2,1)$, $S(2,-2,2)$, $T(1,-3,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{RS}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RS} & =s-r \\\\  & =(2i-2j+2k)-(3i-2j+k) \\\\  & =-i+k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{RT} & =t-r \\\\  & =(i-3j+3k)-(3i-2j+k) \\\\  & =-2i-j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RS}\\times \\overset{\\to }{RT} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1)i-((-1)\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 1)j+((-1)\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =i+k \\\\  & =⟨1,0,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{RS}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{RS}\\times \\overset{\\to }{RT}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,RST$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292815 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47d3a2b5-466f-590c-8ea8-479084264b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47d3a2b5-466f-590c-8ea8-479084264b69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290925} :answer-field/id #uuid "45ec0f2b-c1b4-5c37-a450-1b90d5f71f78" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291960}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41352b96-198e-5a5d-978c-31702eac06ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-275224" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(-2,0,-1)$, $B(-3,3,-4)$, $C(0,-2,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-3i+3j-4k)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =-i+3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-2j+2k)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =2i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot (-3))i-((-1)\\cdot 3-2\\cdot (-3))j+((-1)\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =3i-3j-4k \\\\  & =⟨3,-3,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{34}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{34}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297467 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77b0cc91-ce5c-5046-8f7d-a7344d76cd0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77b0cc91-ce5c-5046-8f7d-a7344d76cd0e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{42}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295920} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ff4772e-9511-5679-8988-c1e0ad78f24a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296670}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e86dffd-3cdd-51b5-8002-a730ad7bd647" :question/math-academy-id "q-316361" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,PQR$, if $P(1,-2,0)$, $Q(3,1,-1)$, $R(-1,0,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(3i+j-k)-(i-2j) \\\\  & =2i+3j-k \\\\  & =⟨2,3,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(-i+2k)-(i-2j) \\\\  & =-2i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 3 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 2)i-(2\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-2))j+(2\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =8i-2j+10k \\\\  & =⟨8,-2,10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{64+4+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{168} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{42}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{42}}{2}=\\sqrt{42}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297468 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dba9f272-6930-502c-8925-212ed902a7be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{237}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296427}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dba9f272-6930-502c-8925-212ed902a7be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{237}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296427} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d733894-4032-579e-a650-81c38b682309" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296890}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a38f6d6d-8117-5b90-a022-c6e9c7160729" :question/math-academy-id "q-316362" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,DEF$, if $D(-2,1,3)$, $E(0,-1,0)$, $F(2,2,-1).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =e-d \\\\  & =(-j)-(-2i+j+3k) \\\\  & =2i-2j-3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =(2i+2j-k)-(-2i+j+3k) \\\\  & =4i+j-4k \\\\  & =⟨4,1,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\times \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot (-4)-(-3)\\cdot 1)i-(2\\cdot (-4)-(-3)\\cdot 4)j+(2\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =11i-4j+10k \\\\  & =⟨11,-4,10⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\times \\overset{\\to }{DF}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{11}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{121+16+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{237}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,DEF$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{237}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297469 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "38ce5de2-b8be-5dc3-beaf-15c0bca7c3b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38ce5de2-b8be-5dc3-beaf-15c0bca7c3b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295588} :answer-field/id #uuid "940eef9e-f927-5a3a-861d-74d1ef0554a6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296940}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "66634719-8e4b-59db-b970-ace87e066b21" :question/math-academy-id "q-316363" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,LMN$, if $L(-3,0,1)$, $M(0,2,-2)$, $N(2,-1,0).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(2j-2k)-(-3i+k) \\\\  & =3i+2j-3k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(2i-j)-(-3i+k) \\\\  & =5i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨5,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot (-1)-(-3)\\cdot (-1))i-(3\\cdot (-1)-(-3)\\cdot 5)j+(3\\cdot (-1)-2\\cdot 5)k \\\\  & =-5i-12j-13k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-12,-13⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-12)^{2}+(-13)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+144+169} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{338} \\\\  & =13\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{13\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297486 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "970f719c-7b09-55f2-929e-43449f0a9042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "970f719c-7b09-55f2-929e-43449f0a9042" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296074} :answer-field/id #uuid "97996f38-e573-5502-9f72-9a2d0b28eaf9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296953}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1c80aa6a-7a46-5942-80d2-93913627438b" :question/math-academy-id "q-316514" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,DEF$, if $D(-1,2,0)$, $E(2,0,1)$, $F(1,3,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =e-d \\\\  & =(2i+k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =3i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =(i+3j+2k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =2i+j+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\times \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)i-(3\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1)j+(3\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-5i-4j+7k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\times \\overset{\\to }{DF}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{90} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,DEF$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297487 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fe7bd94-f1f1-5968-8699-68e5eff1beb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{146}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295726}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fe7bd94-f1f1-5968-8699-68e5eff1beb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{146}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295726} :answer-field/id #uuid "f58dd836-40be-566d-a116-79d128a9ed1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297135}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af1c1af8-7ccd-5f01-9374-729457ea6109" :question/math-academy-id "q-316516" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,LMN$, if $L(1,0,-1)$, $M(3,2,0)$, $N(0,1,3).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(3i+2j)-(i-k) \\\\  & =2i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(j+3k)-(i-k) \\\\  & =-i+j+4k \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 1)i-(2\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot 1)j+(2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =7i-9j+4k \\\\  & =⟨7,-9,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+(-9)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{146}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{146}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297489 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e247391e-4dbd-55f5-93b1-53a444f611d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296472}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e247391e-4dbd-55f5-93b1-53a444f611d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296472} :answer-field/id #uuid "3c517877-5eaa-568b-a6c7-60cea011507e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296751}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf87a92d-df17-5548-a069-1e61f18f426a" :question/math-academy-id "q-316530" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,STU,$ if $S(0,1,2),$ $T(2,3,1),$ $U(4,1,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SU}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ST} & =t-s \\\\  & =(2i+3j+k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{SU} & =u-s \\\\  & =(4i+j+2k)-(j+2k) \\\\  & =4i+0j+0k \\\\  & =⟨4,0,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ST}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SU} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 0)i-(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot 4)j+(2\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =0i-4j-8k \\\\  & =⟨0,-4,-8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{ST}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SU}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{ST}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{80} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,STU$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{4\\sqrt{5}}{2}=2\\sqrt{5}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338894 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "108d7ae9-a232-5e60-a939-66c340b257d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336190} {:answer/id #uuid "4cd5eccf-eb1f-5b09-992c-5886e6477e5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{261}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336746} {:answer/id #uuid "990c829b-454f-5fa4-985e-5a8b68b776dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337424} {:answer/id #uuid "9f98312c-c9f2-57e2-af6f-1c2737cbfe55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{261}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337475} {:answer/id #uuid "e64d8662-a67b-5f89-82e8-43f6670bbf96" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{97}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338040}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cd5eccf-eb1f-5b09-992c-5886e6477e5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{261}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336746} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cc2c532-03ad-50fc-87d1-ea179d58d664" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338436}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "874ee269-4d1d-55a1-8553-04a0864d5dd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71106" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,WXY$, if $W(2,-3,1)$, $X(-2,1,2)$, $Y(3,-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX} & =x-w \\\\  & =(-2i+j+2k)-(2i-3j+k) \\\\  & =-4i+4j+k \\\\  & =⟨-4,4,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =y-w \\\\  & =(3i-j+3k)-(2i-3j+k) \\\\  & =i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2)i-((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)j+((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =6i+9j-12k \\\\  & =⟨6,9,-12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{9}^{2}+{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{261}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,WXY$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{261}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338895 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0932fe92-f8de-576e-baff-260c08cc1de7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336112} {:answer/id #uuid "7efd8fb5-fe32-562c-9d4b-d5fba1fd6b48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337184} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef6d298-4c28-5ba4-8962-81bdffb4b6ad" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337321} {:answer/id #uuid "eb23c031-3731-5c6e-aed8-4d36c5b9f20c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338081} {:answer/id #uuid "fc78233b-b5f1-5862-b741-cfd6e52f48e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338250}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eb23c031-3731-5c6e-aed8-4d36c5b9f20c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338081} :answer-field/id #uuid "0daa5bc7-b875-5ff1-9f3e-508ca3073b43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338302}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0d10b6fa-62e6-5893-8115-0db23250352f" :question/math-academy-id "q-71107" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,NPQ$, if $N(1,0,1)$, $P(2,2,3)$, $Q(2,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{NP}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{NQ}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{NP} & =p-n \\\\  & =(2i+2j+3k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{NQ} & =q-n \\\\  & =(2i+j+k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =i+j \\\\  & =⟨1,1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{NP}\\times \\overset{\\to }{NQ} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2)i-(1\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-2i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{NP}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{NQ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{NP}\\times \\overset{\\to }{NQ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,NPQ$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338896 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3aed134b-e703-50a2-978e-28071145ddef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336586} {:answer/id #uuid "4cfc4a3f-63ff-5d1a-9c0f-ebcdda99431e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336748} {:answer/id #uuid "7047a495-50ca-567e-88e4-273aa8914f6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337028} {:answer/id #uuid "bc4ffce1-6601-5f91-8b10-271b848d8b34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337703} {:answer/id #uuid "ca325988-d63a-57fe-a35a-615af188b50b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337813}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4cfc4a3f-63ff-5d1a-9c0f-ebcdda99431e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336748} :answer-field/id #uuid "40c086ce-f13d-57ca-a69b-b4e1945642fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338395}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d25fe3fb-23c6-5ca6-a0b3-475c85a18297" :question/math-academy-id "q-71109" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,FGH$, if $F(1,1,2)$, $G(2,2,3)$, $H(1,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{FG}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{FH}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FG} & =g-f \\\\  & =(2i+2j+3k)-(i+j+2k) \\\\  & =i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{FH} & =h-f \\\\  & =(i+k)-(i+j+2k) \\\\  & =-j-k \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FG}\\times \\overset{\\to }{FH} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 1)i-(1\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 1)j+(1\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =j-k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{FG}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{FH}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{FG}\\times \\overset{\\to }{FH}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,FGH$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338898 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47e924de-54b8-5328-8007-3b54077fff81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336697} {:answer/id #uuid "55f44d06-e6f6-5fe2-85b3-f7a48edceca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336822} {:answer/id #uuid "d8658307-2241-5976-8f8b-323e902dd088" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337910} {:answer/id #uuid "fc896c2a-9e50-5f5d-a2dd-8fde07578b47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338251} {:answer/id #uuid "fcf6bcc4-3401-51e2-8ab5-cc86c889fcc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338258}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47e924de-54b8-5328-8007-3b54077fff81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336697} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d4de416-4232-5a36-bef2-7154753e04a6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338537}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7c8d8ac3-0a22-56d4-bfd2-5a54455f0999" :question/math-academy-id "q-71111" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,CDE$, if $C(1,-2,3)$, $D(1,-3,3)$, $E(1,1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{CE}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD} & =d-c \\\\  & =(i-3j+3k)-(i-2j+3k) \\\\  & =-j \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{CE} & =e-c \\\\  & =(i+j+k)-(i-2j+3k) \\\\  & =3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,3,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CD}\\times \\overset{\\to }{CE} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-2)-3\\cdot 0)i-(0\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0)j+(0\\cdot 3-0\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =2i \\\\  & =⟨2,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{CD}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{CE}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{CD}\\times \\overset{\\to }{CE}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,CDE$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=1.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105734 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105592 :question/id #uuid "23793048-621c-5ab3-97ac-7e635553c947" :question/math-academy-id "e-4346" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ if $A(-1,1,0),$ $B(1,1,2),$ $C(1,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude (height) can be related to the area of the triangle as follows:\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{b \\cdot h}{2},\n$$\n\n \nwhere $b$ is a base and $h$ is the corresponding altitude of the triangle.\n\nFor the $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC,$ we have $h=CH,$ and $b=AB.$ So, we have\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find $A_{\\bigtriangleup}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(i+j+2k)-(-i+j) \\\\  & =2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(i-j+k)-(-i+j) \\\\  & =2i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))i-(2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 2)j+(2\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =4i+2j-4k \\\\  & =⟨4,2,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $\\bigtriangleup\\!ABC$ is\n\n$$\nA_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2}A = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 6 = 3.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula $A_{\\bigtriangleup} = \\dfrac{1}{2} CH \\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 3 & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b1cac9a-d8ad-501d-b0a6-a0a1bebe9636" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285345} {:answer/id #uuid "3cf88e45-9bac-51c6-a90f-f80f508a8095" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285363} {:answer/id #uuid "46574c64-b2d9-52a5-ba20-5c4e8f687459" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285432} {:answer/id #uuid "61a98581-4f83-59f8-a0f9-f6ec11524a8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285684} {:answer/id #uuid "6cd903e1-1e62-5f4c-86df-6c375dc3361d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b1cac9a-d8ad-501d-b0a6-a0a1bebe9636" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285345} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5b8bbd2-699b-5127-b6f0-02f2e8c72c29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287551}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "95f6f3a1-caa9-5902-b6fb-cb14398f3fb9" :question/math-academy-id "q-20027" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(2,1,2)$, $B(1,2,1)$, $C(3,2,3).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(i+2j+k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =-i+j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(3i+2j+3k)-(2i+j+2k) \\\\  & =i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-1))i-((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot (-1))j+((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =2i-2k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91d02db9-e77b-5b70-bf52-95157c6b371c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{30}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102627} {:answer/id #uuid "b8541fc0-8462-5904-9145-c20fc56387a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102628} {:answer/id #uuid "c06d702c-89e5-5852-9582-6fca6d927ab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102629} {:answer/id #uuid "36fa653c-a96d-5d43-9c00-e68c6671ede2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102630} {:answer/id #uuid "376be9ee-03ee-58c2-9786-34782438fca0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102631}] :answer-field/id #uuid "dc647480-b80a-5e28-afb7-8bed712a7f58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186102626}] :question/id #uuid "74c42862-54b5-59d3-9fc0-d15a552d30c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-20028" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $RH$ of the $△PRQ$, if $P(1,-2, 3)$, $Q(3, 2, 3)$, $R(2, 1, 4)$.\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262863 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "033166a8-eb6e-5026-9379-74758cf8f63e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\sqrt{33}}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186259903} {:answer/id #uuid "46f34cae-0d7f-57af-bd21-c29c4d58eb48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{29}}{29}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260491} {:answer/id #uuid "86df7a60-c683-5984-ab1c-7b2102dfbe16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18\\sqrt{10}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261051} {:answer/id #uuid "8941d219-3334-51f2-895b-7a537acbf651" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{10}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261070} {:answer/id #uuid "c9fd4792-88e8-5bab-8423-291a5ffe487b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18\\sqrt{29}}{29}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261661}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c9fd4792-88e8-5bab-8423-291a5ffe487b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{18\\sqrt{29}}{29}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261661} :answer-field/id #uuid "0af9ae3c-d3ff-5c29-96c7-03340f576f82" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262143}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f3898211-8ec0-5bec-b86d-5fc41284c16c" :question/math-academy-id "q-128006" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC,$ if $A(4,-1,1),$ $B(0,-3,4),$ $C(2,1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-3j+4k)-(4i-j+k) \\\\  & =-4i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+4k)-(4i-j+k) \\\\  & =-2i+2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 3)i-((-4)\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot 3)j+((-4)\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-12i+6j-12k \\\\  & =⟨-12,6,-12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-12)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{324} \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{18}{2}=9.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ 9 & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot \\sqrt{29} \\\\ 18 & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{29} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{29}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{18\\sqrt{29}}{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262864 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17263848-7dad-541b-ad58-74745572f296" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{38}}{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260076} {:answer/id #uuid "1dfb5bcd-7bf0-53b0-a60b-2f17c4f73037" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{38}}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260133} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0f2dce-a930-5b09-bde7-49e546203c40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260526} {:answer/id #uuid "803e61e6-6963-5b24-9fb8-5a3e08371ece" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\sqrt{38}}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260987} {:answer/id #uuid "8d500b7a-085a-5399-943c-18364bfccf23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261108}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "803e61e6-6963-5b24-9fb8-5a3e08371ece" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6\\sqrt{38}}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260987} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8984f2f-6da2-54bf-9096-9f18e7aa0c0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262479}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "dbbc0374-2f40-56ea-b57e-f5227b194e10" :question/math-academy-id "q-128008" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $RH$ of the $△\\,PRQ,$ if $P(3,0,4),$ $Q(2,3,1),$ $R(0,3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $RH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,PQR$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot PQ\n$$\n\nSo, to find $RH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(2i+3j+k)-(3i+4k) \\\\  & =-i+3j-3j \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(3j+k)-(3i+4k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot (-3)-3\\cdot (-3))i-((-1)\\cdot (-3)-(-3)\\cdot (-3))j+((-1)\\cdot 3-(-3)\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =6j+6k \\\\  & =⟨0,6,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{2}=3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $PQ$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}PQ & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot PQ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot PQ \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}RH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ 6\\sqrt{2} & =RH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ RH & =\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\ RH & =\\frac{6\\sqrt{38}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262865 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29485b5b-c665-5779-a34e-0364eb6fa1d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260238} {:answer/id #uuid "4bd34242-8e9e-5678-97c9-7cc01e6d4b3d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260525} {:answer/id #uuid "80b164c6-bba8-504a-bd8b-ab45cf5b2c09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260996} {:answer/id #uuid "83f99092-f762-5530-8c3c-6fee86481012" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261022} {:answer/id #uuid "a02e3ad1-637a-5291-aabd-24871e6db04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261265}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a02e3ad1-637a-5291-aabd-24871e6db04e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261265} :answer-field/id #uuid "658ccd8b-267b-53ca-9ec1-baa7bb2e0bbd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262297}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "acfa5ee8-797a-57cb-8b1c-947581dc04d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-128013" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $MH$ of the $△\\,LMN,$ if $L(-1,4,1),$ $M(0,3,4),$ $N(1,4,2).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $MH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,LMN$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot LN\n$$\n\nSo, to find $MH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(3j+4k)-(-i+4j+k) \\\\  & =i-j+3k \\\\  & =⟨1,-1,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(i+4j+2k)-(-i+4j+k) \\\\  & =2i+k \\\\  & =⟨2,0,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3)i-(1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 3)j+(1\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =-i+5j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-1,5,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{5}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{30}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $LN$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}LN & =|\\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot LN,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot LN \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot \\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{30} & =MH\\cdot \\sqrt{5} \\\\ MH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{30}}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ MH & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292816 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42aac3c5-ad83-55c9-bc67-806f2c57a155" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "42aac3c5-ad83-55c9-bc67-806f2c57a155" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290908} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee54665e-3213-5a19-9284-f386f859abe3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292475}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a1a70e2a-5e7c-521f-a8eb-605197f729a5" :question/math-academy-id "q-275225" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC$, if $A(-2,0,-1)$, $B(0,-2,-1)$, $C(-3,-2,0).$\n\n$CH=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-2j-k)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =2i-2j \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(-3i-2j)-(-2i-k) \\\\  & =-i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 0)i-(2\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)j+(2\\cdot (-2)-(-1)\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-2i-2j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{44} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{11}}{2}=\\sqrt{11}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ \\sqrt{11} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{11} & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{11}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{22}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297473 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c05366e-122f-5432-9545-0905387ebf8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3230}}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295700}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c05366e-122f-5432-9545-0905387ebf8d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3230}}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295700} :answer-field/id #uuid "8653ad62-f824-5e0d-9daf-40a42762bc5c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296909}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cc3dd100-4787-576c-a303-83ee06838d2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-316392" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $NP$ of the $△\\,LMN$, if $L(3,-1,0)$, $M(0,2,1)$, $N(-2,1,-1).$\n\n$NP=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $NP$ can be related to the area of $△\\,LMN$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,NP\\cdot LM.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $NP,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(2j+k)-(3i-j) \\\\  & =-3i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(-2i+j-k)-(3i-j) \\\\  & =-5i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-5,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2)i-((-3)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-5))j+((-3)\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-5))k \\\\  & =-5i-8j+9k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-8,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{170}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $LM$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}LM & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,NP\\cdot LM,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,NP\\cdot LM \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,NP\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ \\sqrt{170} & =NP\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ NP & =\\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3230}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297474 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "285859fd-02f8-5227-baf4-1ae234928772" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4186}}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "285859fd-02f8-5227-baf4-1ae234928772" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{4186}}{14}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295490} :answer-field/id #uuid "96ea95b7-7464-5f8e-b5f7-4c89f5a83900" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296951}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "118c9278-fa2c-5ecd-aadf-b52c033ba66c" :question/math-academy-id "q-316395" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $UT$ of the $△\\,UVW$, if $U(-2,2,0)$, $V(1,-1,2)$, $W(3,0,-1).$\n\n$UT=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $UT$ can be related to the area of $△\\,UVW$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,UT\\cdot VW.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $UT,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{VW}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{VU}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{VW} & =w-v \\\\  & =(3i-k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =2i+j-3k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{VU} & =u-v \\\\  & =(-2i+2j)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{VW}\\times \\overset{\\to }{VU} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot (-2)-(-3)\\cdot 3)i-(2\\cdot (-2)-(-3)\\cdot (-3))j+(2\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-3))k \\\\  & =7i+13j+9k \\\\  & =⟨7,13,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{VW}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{VU}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{VW}\\times \\overset{\\to }{VU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+{13}^{2}+{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{299}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,UVW$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{299}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $VW$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}VW & =|\\overset{\\to }{VW}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,UT\\cdot VW,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,UT\\cdot VW \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{299}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,UT\\cdot \\sqrt{14} \\\\ \\sqrt{299} & =UT\\cdot \\sqrt{14} \\\\ UT & =\\frac{\\sqrt{299}}{\\sqrt{14}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{4186}}{14}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1348e485-5031-58d0-9132-dc7a8e060aa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295371}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1348e485-5031-58d0-9132-dc7a8e060aa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295371} :answer-field/id #uuid "38a7753b-1420-53a5-8abd-6a0b570e42f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296740}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "041de7f5-8dc3-5943-9410-cd670ed64e0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-316400" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $VL$ of the $△\\,TUV$, if $T(1,0,1)$, $U(3,2,-1)$, $V(-1,1,0).$\n\n$VL=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $VL$ can be related to the area of $△\\,TUV$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot TU\n$$\n\nSo, to find $VL,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{TU}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TV}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TU} & =u-t \\\\  & =(3i+2j-k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =2i+2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{TV} & =v-t \\\\  & =(-i+j)-(i+k) \\\\  & =-2i+j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 1)i-(2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot (-2))j+(2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =0i+6j+6k \\\\  & =⟨0,6,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{TU}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TV}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,TUV$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{2}=3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $TU$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TU & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot TU,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot TU \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =VL\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ VL & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ VL & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297477 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff61a221-719e-515d-a51f-fa366df765f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296631}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff61a221-719e-515d-a51f-fa366df765f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296631} :answer-field/id #uuid "49802bb4-f9df-54ac-8e86-92d7c96102d2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296770}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0e0cc38a-3052-5bd2-aef9-6d95ea796618" :question/math-academy-id "q-316409" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $IP$ of the $△\\,HIJ$, if $H(-1,2,0)$, $I(1,1,3)$, $J(0,-2,1).$\n\n$IP=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $IP$ can be related to the area of $△\\,HIJ$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}IP\\cdot HJ\n$$\n\nSo, to find $IP,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{HI}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HJ} & =j-h \\\\  & =(-2j+k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =i-4j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,-4,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{HI} & =i-h \\\\  & =(i+j+3k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =2i-j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,-1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{HJ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{HI} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1))i-(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot (-1)-(-4)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-11i-j+7k \\\\  & =⟨-11,-1,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{HJ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{HI}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{HJ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{HI}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-11)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{171} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,HIJ$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{19}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $HJ$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}HJ & =|\\overset{\\to }{HJ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}IP\\cdot HJ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}IP\\cdot HJ \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{19}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,IP\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{19} & =\\sqrt{2}\\,IP \\\\ IP & =\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297491 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a47b6ed-480c-5e70-aefa-cd3ffcab87ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{806}}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a47b6ed-480c-5e70-aefa-cd3ffcab87ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{806}}{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186295507} :answer-field/id #uuid "fd373048-f3c1-5400-8d49-9bc5ec200162" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297153}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3aadd472-6c53-5587-bcdd-18195d95d688" :question/math-academy-id "q-316553" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $CK$ of the $△\\,ABC,$ if $A(1,0,1),$ $B(4,2,1),$ $C(2,3,2).$\n\n$CK=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $CK$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CK\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CK,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(4i+2j+k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =3i+2j+0k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(2i+3j+2k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,3,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3)i-(3\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1)j+(3\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =2i-3j+7k \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{62}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CK\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}CK\\cdot \\sqrt{13} \\\\ CK & =\\frac{\\sqrt{62}}{\\sqrt{13}} \\\\ CK & =\\frac{\\sqrt{806}}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297492 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7fbf2db-fc7b-5658-bc9b-3b51bd33b591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{110}}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296318}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7fbf2db-fc7b-5658-bc9b-3b51bd33b591" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{110}}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296318} :answer-field/id #uuid "659b57b6-4355-5ee2-9530-0067f725247f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296845}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9fd89971-85c9-5581-b57b-a897961ff335" :question/math-academy-id "q-316556" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $HK$ of the $△\\,GHI,$ if $G(1,1,1),$ $H(3,2,4),$ $I(2,4,2).$\n\n$HK=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $HK$ can be related to the area of $△\\,GHI$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}HK\\cdot GI\n$$\n\nSo, to find $HK,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{GI}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{GH}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{GI} & =i-g \\\\  & =(2i+4j+2k)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,3,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{GH} & =h-g \\\\  & =(3i+2j+4k)-(i+j+k) \\\\  & =2i+j+3k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{GI}\\times \\overset{\\to }{GH} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 1)i-(1\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =8i-j-5k \\\\  & =⟨8,-1,-5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{GI}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{GH}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{GI}\\times \\overset{\\to }{GH}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-5)^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,GHI$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $GI$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}GI & =|\\overset{\\to }{GI}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}HK\\cdot GI,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}HK\\cdot \\sqrt{11} \\\\ HK & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\ HK & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{110}}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186297493 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8a61533-070f-501b-8382-171a4281490f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{22}}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8a61533-070f-501b-8382-171a4281490f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{22}}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296320} :answer-field/id #uuid "51a19f72-85aa-5439-92e2-7ba79108e904" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186296795}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "05e91010-8b10-50cc-b3a2-21f43d310a7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-316558" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $TK$ of the $△\\,RST,$ if $R(4,5,6),$ $S(7,4,5),$ $T(6,8,4).$\n\n$TK=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $TK$ can be related to the area of $△\\,RST$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}TK\\cdot RS\n$$\n\nSo, to find $TK,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{RS}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RS} & =s-r \\\\  & =(7i+4j+5k)-(4i+5j+6k) \\\\  & =3i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{RT} & =t-r \\\\  & =(6i+8j+4k)-(4i+5j+6k) \\\\  & =2i+3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨2,3,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RS}\\times \\overset{\\to }{RT} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)(-2)-(-1)\\cdot 3)i-(3(-2)-(-1)\\cdot 2)j+(3\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =5i+4j+11k \\\\  & =⟨5,4,11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{RS}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{RS}\\times \\overset{\\to }{RT}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{11}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{162} \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,RST$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $RS$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RS & =|\\overset{\\to }{RS}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}TK\\cdot RS,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}TK\\cdot \\sqrt{11} \\\\ TK & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\ TK & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{22}}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338899 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2bce9a27-f4cc-58b8-899b-0adcf77a3029" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336444} {:answer/id #uuid "3154ea6f-18ff-5b87-b29e-4d415f805d06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336503} {:answer/id #uuid "8127319e-f64a-5b03-9442-11dd8802bec3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337204} {:answer/id #uuid "9c703731-367d-5c95-8dba-8382da5e1070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337446} {:answer/id #uuid "9ccd42e4-4e86-5ccb-92e1-e81125b47e32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337449}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c703731-367d-5c95-8dba-8382da5e1070" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337446} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b6a4426-4d5c-5b55-8aaf-f5663e17d82d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338434}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2109dfb7-8989-5063-a0ad-becd345c3aae" :question/math-academy-id "q-71113" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $MH$ of the $△\\,LMN$, if $L(3,3,2)$, $M(1,1,2)$, $N(2,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $MH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,LMN$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot LN\n$$\n\nSo, to find $MH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(i+j+2k)-(3i+3j+2k) \\\\  & =-2i-2j \\\\  & =⟨-2,-2,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(2i+2j+k)-(3i+3j+2k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0)i-((-2)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 0)j+((-2)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =2i-2j \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $LN$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}LN & =|\\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot LN,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot LN \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}MH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & =MH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ MH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ MH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338900 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "072d3204-08b4-5aac-aca7-bdc773125774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{38}}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336085} {:answer/id #uuid "62d5a2fd-d0ed-50a1-b9e1-530565c72f2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336920} {:answer/id #uuid "8101cc36-fb71-50d7-ac71-47da39f98581" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337201} {:answer/id #uuid "b2d8bec1-6d0d-54d7-ae45-5d08e1b8540e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337627} {:answer/id #uuid "e626fb9e-e952-533a-955b-4d34b400fc65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338039}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "072d3204-08b4-5aac-aca7-bdc773125774" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{38}}{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336085} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2232b9a-6e70-56f9-95d7-f89ee74428fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338675}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "86adad36-11f0-5e43-80fd-01317a16e7e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-71115" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $VH$ of the $△\\,TUV$, if $T(3,2,3)$, $U(0,1,0)$, $V(2,1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $VH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,TUV$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VH\\cdot TU\n$$\n\nSo, to find $VH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{TU}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TV}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TU} & =u-t \\\\  & =j-(3i+2j+3k) \\\\  & =-3i-j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-1,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{TV} & =v-t \\\\  & =(2i+j+2k)-(3i+2j+3k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-3))i-((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-3))j+((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =-2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,0,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{TU}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TV}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,TUV$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $TU$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TU & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VH\\cdot TU,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}VH\\cdot TU \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}VH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & =VH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ VH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\ VH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{38}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338901 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "093467b9-0067-542c-b65c-633c1cfc4b53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336113} {:answer/id #uuid "3859e15a-56e5-569e-825a-f822ed3eac71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336557} {:answer/id #uuid "6c2eb1b1-c7b8-5381-b418-d9244be8d489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336991} {:answer/id #uuid "d8d294a1-32a0-5b4f-94b7-ee30ffc9011a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337918} {:answer/id #uuid "de85db2c-4065-5f60-92b7-7fdad6d31158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337972}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d8d294a1-32a0-5b4f-94b7-ee30ffc9011a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337918} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d1b4065-470d-599f-81c3-c9f0fd87b16f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338536}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9999542b-9f9f-5d86-95f6-bcd8d4190efb" :question/math-academy-id "q-71116" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $ZH$ of the $△\\,WYZ$, if $W(2,3,2)$, $Y(1,2,1)$, $Z(1,-1,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $ZH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,WYZ$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}ZH\\cdot WY\n$$\n\nSo, to find $ZH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WZ}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WY} & =y-w \\\\  & =(i+2j+k)-(2i+3j+2k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{WZ} & =z-w \\\\  & =(i-j+k)-(2i+3j+2k) \\\\  & =-i-4j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-4,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WY}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WZ} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-1)-(-4)\\cdot (-1))i-((-1)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-1))j+((-1)\\cdot (-4)-(-1)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =-3i+3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WZ}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{WY}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WZ}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,WYZ$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $WY$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}WY & =|\\overset{\\to }{WY}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}ZH\\cdot WY,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}ZH\\cdot WY \\\\ \\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}ZH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =ZH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ ZH & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ ZH & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338902 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06d340e7-ddb4-51cf-bbf6-01458c17f611" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336084} {:answer/id #uuid "0d900ac9-ddc4-5d0b-8b81-7b341697e575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336159} {:answer/id #uuid "56354dd4-647e-56d7-a9fd-a95bbb4ca8e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336825} {:answer/id #uuid "8125d199-48f3-5aad-b0c5-ab92c3d59078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337203} {:answer/id #uuid "fa8b3bae-3fde-5b2f-8f26-3e3448abad77" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{38}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8125d199-48f3-5aad-b0c5-ab92c3d59078" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337203} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e6e1490-16c3-533e-862d-6938fcc3b920" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338333}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f34d7ce2-3b18-5fda-a701-f95afc0575b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71117" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $GH$ of the $△\\,GSM$, if $S(1,-1,2)$, $G(-2,0,2)$, $M(1,1,0).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $GH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,GSM$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}GH\\cdot SM\n$$\n\nSo, to find $GH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{SG}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SM}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SG} & =g-s \\\\  & =(-2i+2k)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =-3i+j \\\\  & =⟨-3,1,0⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{SM} & =m-s \\\\  & =(i+j)-(i-j+2k) \\\\  & =2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{SG}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SM} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 0)i-((-3)\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0)j+((-3)\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =-2i-6j-6k \\\\  & =⟨-2,-6,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{SG}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{SM}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{SG}\\times \\overset{\\to }{SM}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-6)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{76} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,GSM$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{19}}{2}=\\sqrt{19}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $SM$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}SM & =|\\overset{\\to }{SM}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}GH\\cdot SM,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}GH\\cdot SM \\\\ \\sqrt{19} & =\\frac{1}{2}GH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{19} & =GH\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\ GH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ GH & =\\frac{\\sqrt{38}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338904 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f3c7d45-2508-558a-a671-704a2f709aa7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186336627} {:answer/id #uuid "733fefab-043d-5fe4-93ed-cf5c6a3298cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337070} {:answer/id #uuid "ca0454d2-6cd6-50e2-9a7f-17ac15f3a137" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337812} {:answer/id #uuid "d3fb8394-0a4f-5554-bef2-b4565678aeac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337886} {:answer/id #uuid "f7adc41f-f450-52b1-9898-009b7b23875a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3fb8394-0a4f-5554-bef2-b4565678aeac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337886} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1e3142c-b7af-51c6-a353-db8d28d28403" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338622}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6da0a984-327a-597f-9055-73fa298d90dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-71128" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $DH$ of the $△\\,DMA$, if $D(-1,2,1)$, $M(-1,0,-1)$, $A(1,-2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $DH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,DMA$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}DH\\cdot MA\n$$\n\nSo, to find $DH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{MD}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{MA}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{MD} & =d-m \\\\  & =(-i+2j+k)-(-i-k) \\\\  & =2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨0,2,2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{MA} & =a-m \\\\  & =(i-2j+k)-(-i-k) \\\\  & =2i-2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{MD}\\times \\overset{\\to }{MA} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot 2)i-(0\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 2)j+(0\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =8i+4j-4k \\\\  & =⟨8,4,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{MD}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{MA}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{MD}\\times \\overset{\\to }{MA}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{8}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{96} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,DMA$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{4\\sqrt{6}}{2}=2\\sqrt{6}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $MA$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}MA & =|\\overset{\\to }{MA}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}DH\\cdot MA,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}DH\\cdot MA \\\\ 2\\sqrt{6} & =\\frac{1}{2}DH\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{6} & =DH\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ DH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ DH & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Altitude of a Triangle Given Its Vertices"}]}
